WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.387
A much shorter

00:00:01.199 --> 00:00:02.095
Lean proof of

00:00:01.907 --> 00:00:03.463
the Riemann Hypothesis

00:00:03.990 --> 00:00:04.673
This is a

00:00:04.485 --> 00:00:05.640
Lean 4 proof

00:00:05.488 --> 00:00:06.254
of the Riemann

00:00:06.065 --> 00:00:07.032
Hypothesis

00:00:07.068 --> 00:00:08.223
and the Generalized

00:00:08.035 --> 00:00:09.367
Riemann Hypothesis

00:00:09.179 --> 00:00:10.888
for Dirichlet L-functions

00:00:11.422 --> 00:00:12.141
It is built

00:00:11.953 --> 00:00:13.120
on Mathlib and

00:00:12.931 --> 00:00:14.098
uses only three

00:00:13.910 --> 00:00:14.688
axioms

00:00:14.771 --> 00:00:15.749
and it follows

00:00:15.561 --> 00:00:17.070
Levent Alpoge's approach

00:00:16.882 --> 00:00:17.672
in a shorter

00:00:17.483 --> 00:00:18.650
version made with

00:00:18.497 --> 00:00:19.782
Anthropic colleagues

00:00:19.594 --> 00:00:20.372
and Claude

00:00:20.894 --> 00:00:21.778
A build takes

00:00:21.590 --> 00:00:22.261
one to two

00:00:22.073 --> 00:00:23.063
hours on twelve

00:00:22.875 --> 00:00:24.172
cores with twenty-four

00:00:23.984 --> 00:00:25.221
gigabytes of memory

00:00:25.399 --> 00:00:26.695
or about eighty-five

00:00:26.507 --> 00:00:27.627
minutes more without

00:00:27.439 --> 00:00:28.511
the Mathlib cache

00:00:29.046 --> 00:00:30.060
Full story on

00:00:29.871 --> 00:00:30.767
the dashboard
